/// [Seller Business Profile Model] - This implements the seller business profile requirement from the Seller/Admin Management specification (see onboarding, compliance, and privilege separation section in the requirements analysis).
///
/// This model stores structured business profile details for each seller to facilitate onboarding, verification and regulatory compliance. Maintains 3NF normalization by separating business information from user accounts/identity details, ensuring adaptability to various business registration workflows. For example, it is used to store business registration info, tax ID, company details, and state throughout onboarding.
///
/// Key relationships: references ai_ecommerce_sellers for its 1:1 link to the seller. Referenced by ai_ecommerce_seller_onboarding_logs and ai_ecommerce_seller_verification_documents for audit compliance tracking.
/// Special behaviors: Only one business profile per seller. Profile can be soft-deleted and must be auditable for compliance.
///
/// @namespace SellerAdmin
/// @author AutoBE - https://github.com/wrtnlabs/autobe
model ai_ecommerce_seller_business_profiles {
  //----
  // COLUMNS
  //----
  /// [Primary key] - Uniquely identifies the seller business profile record. Implements the business profile requirement for unique, auditable identification of seller registration data. Required for normalized, atomic key structure.
  id String @id @db.Uuid

  /// [Seller linkage] - Links to ai_ecommerce_sellers. Implements requirement to associate each business profile to the seller account. Maintains normalization by storing only the reference, not duplicated seller data. For example, used during onboarding or audits to fetch the seller.
  seller_id String @db.Uuid

  /// [Business name] - Implements business identification aspect. The registered name of seller's company. Ensures atomicity and separation from user identity.
  business_name String

  /// [Business reg. number] - Implements regulatory compliance. Stores the unique government-issued business number. Required for audit. 3NF: all business info relates only to its own profile.
  business_registration_number String

  /// [Tax ID] - Implements taxation compliance requirement. Holds unique business tax identifier. Maintains normalized, atomic structure and ensures auditability.
  tax_id String?

  /// [Contact name] - Implements business contact point. The official representative for business queries. Keeps contact data atomic, separated from business legal records.
  contact_name String

  /// [Contact phone] - Implements primary contact info. Used for onboarding, support, and compliance calls. Properly atomic with no embedded objects.
  contact_phone String

  /// [Contact email] - Implements contact traceability requirement. Business communication endpoint. Not user email, always business-specific. Properly normalized.
  contact_email String

  /// [Business address 1] - Implements physical presence requirement. First address line. Kept atomic to meet normalization. No embedded geolocations.
  address_line1 String

  /// [Business address 2] - Optional second line for complex addresses. Normalized field, null if unused.
  address_line2 String?

  /// [Business city] - Implements location detail aspect. Atomic, normalized for city search/filtering.
  city String

  /// [Business state/province] - Required for legal correspondence and filtering. Separate from city for normalization.
  state String

